2025-05-01 03:34:39 - Thread-1531 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

Match  
• "season": season that each game belongs to – will be our main grouping unit.  
• "league_id": foreign‑key to League, lets us know which league the match is in.  
• "country_id": foreign‑key to Country, ultimately gives us the nation of the league.  
• "home_team_api_id" / "away_team_api_id": the two competitors – link to Team table.  
• "home_team_goal" / "away_team_goal": final score.  Used to decide win / draw / loss and therefore the number of points.  

Team  
• "team_api_id": joins to the two team columns above.  
• "team_long_name": readable team name for the output champion list.  

League  
• "id": joins to Match."league_id".  
• "name": readable league name for the output.  

Country  
• "id": joins to Match."country_id".  
• "name": readable country name for the output.  

Typical conditions / logic we will need  
1. CASE expression to turn a single match into points for each side:  
   – home win → 3 pts for home_team_api_id, 0 pts for away_team_api_id  
   – away win → 0 / 3 respectively  
   – draw     → 1 / 1  
2. GROUP BY "season", "league_id", "team_api_id" to sum the points.  
3. Within each ("season","league_id") pick the team that has the MAX points.  
4. Join to Team, League, Country for friendly names.

Below are 10 exploratory SQL queries, from simple look‑ups to an almost‑final champion computation.  
(Every query is limited to 20 rows to keep the result small.)

```sql
-- 1. Seasons available in the data
SELECT DISTINCT "season"
FROM "Match"
ORDER BY "season"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Leagues present (id + name)
SELECT DISTINCT l."id", l."name"
FROM "League" AS l
ORDER BY l."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Countries present (id + name)
SELECT DISTINCT c."id", c."name"
FROM "Country" AS c
ORDER BY c."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect a few raw match score lines
SELECT "id",
       "season",
       "league_id",
       "home_team_api_id",
       "home_team_goal",
       "away_team_api_id",
       "away_team_goal"
FROM "Match"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Same as above but with readable team & league names
SELECT m."season",
       l."name"  AS "league",
       th."team_long_name" AS "home_team",
       m."home_team_goal",
       ta."team_long_name" AS "away_team",
       m."away_team_goal"
FROM "Match"           AS m
LEFT JOIN "Team"   AS th ON th."team_api_id" = m."home_team_api_id"
LEFT JOIN "Team"   AS ta ON ta."team_api_id" = m."away_team_api_id"
LEFT JOIN "League" AS l  ON l."id"          = m."league_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Derive points earned in each match for both sides (one row per match)
SELECT m."id",
       CASE
         WHEN m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal" THEN 3
         WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
         ELSE 0
       END AS "home_pts",
       CASE
         WHEN m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal" THEN 3
         WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
         ELSE 0
       END AS "away_pts"
FROM "Match" AS m
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Unpivot the previous result: one row per team per match with its points
SELECT m."season",
       m."league_id",
       m."home_team_api_id"  AS "team_api_id",
       CASE
         WHEN m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal" THEN 3
         WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
         ELSE 0
       END AS "points"
FROM "Match" AS m
UNION ALL
SELECT m."season",
       m."league_id",
       m."away_team_api_id",
       CASE
         WHEN m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal" THEN 3
         WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
         ELSE 0
       END
FROM "Match" AS m
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Aggregate total points of every team within each season & league
SELECT tp."season",
       tp."league_id",
       tp."team_api_id",
       SUM(tp."points") AS "total_points"
FROM (
        -- same UNION ALL block as in query 7
        SELECT m."season",
               m."league_id",
               m."home_team_api_id"  AS "team_api_id",
               CASE
                 WHEN m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal" THEN 3
                 WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
                 ELSE 0
               END AS "points"
        FROM "Match" AS m
        UNION ALL
        SELECT m."season",
               m."league_id",
               m."away_team_api_id",
               CASE
                 WHEN m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal" THEN 3
                 WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
                 ELSE 0
               END
        FROM "Match" AS m
     ) AS tp
GROUP BY tp."season", tp."league_id", tp."team_api_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Find, for each (season, league), the maximum points tally
SELECT ap."season",
       ap."league_id",
       MAX(ap."total_points") AS "max_pts"
FROM (
      /* aggregated table from query 8 */
      SELECT tp."season",
             tp."league_id",
             tp."team_api_id",
             SUM(tp."points") AS "total_points"
      FROM (
              SELECT m."season",
                     m."league_id",
                     m."home_team_api_id"  AS "team_api_id",
                     CASE
                       WHEN m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal" THEN 3
                       WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
                       ELSE 0
                     END AS "points"
              FROM "Match" AS m
              UNION ALL
              SELECT m."season",
                     m."league_id",
                     m."away_team_api_id",
                     CASE
                       WHEN m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal" THEN 3
                       WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
                       ELSE 0
                     END
              FROM "Match" AS m
           ) AS tp
      GROUP BY tp."season", tp."league_id", tp."team_api_id"
) AS ap
GROUP BY ap."season", ap."league_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final: champion team of every season (all leagues & countries) with names
WITH team_points AS (
    -- aggregated points per team/season/league
    SELECT tp."season",
           tp."league_id",
           tp."team_api_id",
           SUM(tp."points") AS "total_points"
    FROM (
            SELECT m."season",
                   m."league_id",
                   m."home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
                   CASE
                     WHEN m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal" THEN 3
                     WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
                     ELSE 0
                   END AS "points"
            FROM "Match" AS m
            UNION ALL
            SELECT m."season",
                   m."league_id",
                   m."away_team_api_id",
                   CASE
                     WHEN m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal" THEN 3
                     WHEN m."home_team_goal" = m."away_team_goal" THEN 1
                     ELSE 0
                   END
            FROM "Match" AS m
         ) AS tp
    GROUP BY tp."season", tp."league_id", tp."team_api_id"
),
ranked AS (
    SELECT t1.*,
           RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t1."season", t1."league_id"
                        ORDER BY t1."total_points" DESC) AS rn
    FROM team_points AS t1
)
SELECT r."season",
       lg."name"   AS "league",
       c."name"    AS "country",
       tm."team_long_name" AS "champion_team",
       r."total_points"
FROM   ranked AS r
JOIN   "Team"   AS tm ON tm."team_api_id" = r."team_api_id"
JOIN   "League" AS lg ON lg."id"         = r."league_id"
JOIN   "Country" AS c ON c."id"          = lg."country_id"
WHERE  r.rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

(The last query yields the champion team for each season/league/country, capped at 20 seasons for brevity.)
